// b: edges { … }` yields two entries both named "edges". The walkers switch on
// Name and every non-column arm assigns, so without this collapse the last
// alias would win and the others would render off columns the SELECT never
// fetched. Coalescing first restores the invariant the arms are
// written against: each name is handled exactly once, over everything every
// alias of it asked for.
